# Why can't I do this? (2)

### Question

I'm trying to do this:

\documentclass{article}

\begin{document}

\section{First}
\section{Second}
\section{Third}

\end{document}


But I'm getting this error:

! LaTeX Error: Something's wrong--perhaps a missing \item.

See the LaTeX manual or LaTeX Companion for explanation.
Type  H <return>  for immediate help.
...

l.4 \section{Second}


What's wrong?

### 1 Answer

The \section command does not start a list environment. You need to start a new paragraph.

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
\section{First}

\section{Second}

\section{Third}
\end{document}


Alternatively, you could use \paragraph instead of \section, which does start a list environment.

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
\paragraph{First}

\paragraph{Second}

\paragraph{Third}
\end{document}
